A3. Intake channels
Guidance: One row per channel, not per L3. Where a link is referenced in the input, record what sits behind it and attach a screenshot. Request real input files (emails, Excel files, message extracts, forms) covering the clean case, the messy case, and at least one that was rejected or returned, with a minimum of 5 to 10 per input pattern.
Ch #	Input pattern	Mailbox address / queue / feed / system	Sender profile	Links referenced in the input and what sits behind them	Attachment types	Template fixed or free-form	Real input files: count, provided by, by when
							
							
							
							
							
							
A4. Trigger and intent identification
Guidance: Out of everything arriving on this channel, how does the analyst know an item belongs to this L2, and then to which L3? Answer per channel. This is an L2-level question because the item arrives before anyone knows which L3 it is.
Channel	How the item is recognised as belonging to this activity (subject line, keyword, request type, message type, file name, sender group, read the body)	Signal reliability H/M/L	What the analyst does when it is ambiguous	Can one item map to multiple L3s? Y/N	If yes: how often, and how is it split today	Handled by one person or routed to several
						
						
						
						
						
						
A5. Systems landscape
Guidance: Every system touched anywhere in this L2. Access method and constraints are recorded here because they determine what is feasible later, and they are the items with the longest lead time.
System	Role in this activity	Read / Write	Access method available today (UI only, API, file drop, none)	Owner team	Internal or third party	Known access, licensing or technical constraints
						
						
						
						
						
						
						
						
						
						
A6. Existing automation
Guidance: Any macro, EUC, RPA bot, Excel tool, workflow rule, Power Automate flow or script already in use. What it does not cover is usually more informative than what it does.
Automation name	Type	L3s covered	What it does	What it does not cover	Built by	Maintained by	Registered / approved Y/N
							
							
							
							
							
							

 Part B — L3 Activity Form
