Guidance: Complete only where this L3 differs from the channels recorded in Part A, Section A3. Leave blank if it follows the L2 default.
Channel (from A3)	Difference for this L3	Notes
		
		
		
B3. As-is process steps and decision rules
Guidance: One row per step as performed today. The last three columns apply only to steps that involve a judgement; leave them blank for pure execution steps. Capture the decision rule in the words the SME uses, and state where it is written down. Where it is written down nowhere, record "tacit". Every numeric limit needs a named owner, otherwise it will surface later as an unresolved item.
Step #	Action performed	System(s) used	Performer role	M / S / A	Shared step? Y + name	Decision rule as stated by the SME, and where it is documented	Thresholds and limits, with owner of each number	Exception, escalation or return-to-requester trigger
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
								
Guidance: M = fully manual, S = semi-automated (a tool assists but a person drives), A = fully automated today.
B4. Current maker-checker process
Guidance: Record what happens today, not what should happen. Where there is no second check, say so explicitly.
Who prepares the change (maker), and role	
Whose credentials the maker acts on	
Who checks it, and role	
Whose credentials the checker acts on	
What triggers a check (all cases, value threshold, sampling, risk rating)	
Check coverage: 100% or sampled, and the sampling basis	
What evidence the checker looks at	
What happens on rejection, and who it goes back to	
Where the approval is recorded	
Any additional approver or authoriser, and what triggers them	
Any step performed today with no second check	
B5. Systems used by this L3
Guidance: Reference systems from the Part A list rather than re-describing them. Record only which ones this L3 touches and where.
System (from A5)	Used at step #	Read / Write	Notes specific to this L3
			
			
			
			
			
			
			
B6. Existing automation covering this L3
Automation (from A6)	Steps covered	What it does not cover for this L3
		
		
		
		
B7. Pain points and failure modes
Guidance: Where rework happens, the most common error, what causes a break, backlog behaviour, and seasonality. Tie each to a step number so it can be traced.
Pain point or failure mode	Step #	Frequency	Impact	Current workaround
				
				
				
				
				
				
				
				
