 Example — Part B, Section B1. Identification and effort
L3 reference and name	2.1, Counterparty drafts a new email with single or multiple trade details in the body
Parent L2 reference and name	OTC Settlements Compare and Match
One-line description	A counterparty initiates a new email to the shared mailbox asserting trade details, which the analyst locates and reconciles against Nomura records before acting
Same as (another L3), and the difference	Not applicable. L3 3.1 is the closest, differing only in that the trades arrive in an Excel attachment rather than the body.
Volume, stating the period	15 to 18 unstructured cashflows per analyst per business day, combined across themes; the 2.1-specific split is open with Haris Raza
Frequency and peak / seasonal pattern	Daily. Volumes rise significantly from the 20th of the last month of each quarter, on contract expiries, and in the first week of each month.
Average handling time per case	10 to 20 minutes per cashflow
Number of people performing it, and FTE effort	OTC Settlements analyst team; FTE split by L3 not separately measured
TAT or SLA, and how it is measured	Ageing buckets T+0, T+1, T+2 and beyond; ageing breach rate is not measured today
In scope Y/N, and rationale	Yes. Free-form counterparty correspondence represents the upper bound of complexity in this space and is the highest-volume unstructured path.
